{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fa7dac5c9164e910492037a9da4cc14a3bcbe81ade5571a26ce67b058592b496","digest":{"component_or_area":"terraform-drift workflow and Gerrit CI integration","key_entities":[".github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml","infra/terraform/**","infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md","infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","terraform plan","-detailed-exitcode","aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm","monitoring_autodeploy.tf","e9d4d390c3"],"problem_keywords":["terraform drift","un-applied infrastructure","gerrit ci gap","pre-submit gate","change verification"],"propositions":["Gerrit changes do not trigger the terraform-drift workflow because Gerrit flows through GitHub as a mirror and does not emit pull_request or push-to-main events.","The terraform-drift check runs post-merge, after a change is submitted to main, so Verified gate carries no signal about whether terraform resources were actually applied.","A terraform change can pass CI and be submitted despite containing un-applied HCL, leaving infrastructure declared in code but absent in AWS.","Manual terraform applies are separate from code merge, creating a gap where landing and applying are distinct acts that CI does not enforce together."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787391438472758001,"uuid":"66985acf-0f17-4c07-ad6a-fb7413359a97"}